module
public import Theory.Mathieu.M24.LocalGeometry.SylowNormalizer.Order

/-!
# A noncommuting cover of the M24 Sylow involutions

The square-one elements of the existing certified Sylow enumeration are
partitioned into 64 parts. Distinct elements of each part fail to commute, so
an elementary abelian subgroup meets each part in at most one element.
Repeated entries pad the short parts and do not affect this property.

The tables are untrusted data, generated by `source/generate.py`; the Lean
kernel checks both coverage and noncommutation against the original native
Sylow elements. No new group model or subgroup classification is assumed.

Source application: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
G.7.3(2), printed p.348, using the rank references on printed p.347.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Sporadic.Mathieu.SmallModuleRanks.M24Certificate
open Sporadic.Mathieu.M24LocalGeometry.SylowNormalizer.OrderEnumeration
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

